      <div class="msv__faq">
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Does UK pension increase when I live abroad?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">YES—Spain is unique. UK state pensions ARE uprated annually in Spain thanks to the Brexit Withdrawal Agreement. In many countries (Canada, Australia), pensions freeze. Spain is one of the few countries where UK pensions continue to increase with UK inflation.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ How do I get UK pension paid to Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Contact the UK Pension Service and notify them you're moving to Spain. Provide your Spanish address. You can arrange direct deposit to a Spanish bank account or receive UK cheques mailed to Spain (slower). Direct deposit is faster—takes 2-4 weeks.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Is UK pension taxable in Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Yes. UK state pension is fully taxable in Spain as income. Private pension withdrawals are also taxable. Under the UK-Spain tax treaty, the UK typically has taxing rights on UK pensions, reducing Spanish tax burden. The tax rate depends on your total income (19% to 47%).</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ What is the S1 form?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">The S1 form entitles UK pensioners to free healthcare in Spain through the public system. You must be receiving a UK pension. Apply through the UK Overseas Healthcare Services. Once approved, register with Spanish healthcare and access equivalent NHS services at no cost.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Do I need to notify HMRC I'm moving?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Yes. Notify HMRC that you're moving abroad. Provide your Spanish address. You remain UK tax resident even in Spain if you have significant UK ties. You'll likely file UK taxes on any UK-source income (UK property, UK pension). Notify them to update records.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ What about private pensions?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Private UK pensions (drawdown, annuities) are taxable in Spain. Withdrawals are fully taxable income. You must declare them on Spanish tax return. The UK-Spain treaty usually allows UK to tax pension income. Currency exchange rates matter for Pound-to-Euro conversion.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
